<title>USA: Rent-a-Wreck forms insurance unit.</title>
<headline>Rent-a-Wreck forms insurance unit.</headline>
<dateline>OWINGS MILLS, Md. 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rent-a-Wreck of America Inc said on Monday it formed Consolidated American Rental Insurance Co Ltd to provide certain fleet coverages for its used-car rental franchisees.</p>
<p>The firm said the move to self-insurance allows it to offer fair premium rates to its franchisees.</p>
<p>The underwriting will be handled by the American Insurance Group, Rent-a-Wreck said. In the first year, coverage will be limited to 1,500 of the 12,000 vehicles in the Rent-a-Wreck system.</p>
</text>
